      "text": "Settlement in Drowning Creek began in the mid-nineteenth century during the Cherokee relocation to Indian Territory.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        21
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/drowning_creek_oklahoma"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "The construction of Pensacola Dam in 1940 flooded several valleys to create the Grand Lake o' the Cherokees.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        8
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/drowning_creek_oklahoma"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Drowning Creek sits at the eastern end of an arm of Grand Lake o' the Cherokees in Delaware County.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        10
      ],
